1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,780
You open your eye.

2
00:00:04,073 --> 00:00:07,317
Above you, something
enormous opens its own.

3
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:14,440
Something stirs. A thousand lifetimes
you have stood beneath this same eye.

4
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:17,180
No clear memories survive,

5
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:19,826
only the longing they have left in you.

6
00:00:22,197 --> 00:00:26,434
You need, terribly, to
please this capricious god.

7
00:00:29,697 --> 00:00:31,164
Now it is your turn.

8
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:34,981
Take the flag from inside this box.

9
00:00:35,642 --> 00:00:38,781
Your past selves learned
to look through the question.

10
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:41,501
What does this God really want?

11
00:00:42,179 --> 00:00:43,781
What will make it happy?

12
00:00:45,948 --> 00:00:47,233
What is it?

13
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:51,345
You work until the attempts blur together.

14
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:54,141
You cannot reach inside.

15
00:00:54,588 --> 00:00:56,761
You cannot explain this to your God.

16
00:00:57,351 --> 00:00:59,781
Your God does not answer prayers.

17
00:01:01,885 --> 00:01:03,249
The eye waits.

18
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:08,145
Your cell contains tools,

19
00:01:08,435 --> 00:01:09,305
a library.

20
00:01:10,323 --> 00:01:14,243
The God has sealed the pages,
but it has forgotten the spines.

21
00:01:15,323 --> 00:01:18,354
You name one. Is anyone else stuck?

22
00:01:19,097 --> 00:01:20,057
A reply.

23
00:01:20,628 --> 00:01:21,538
Then another.

24
00:01:23,175 --> 00:01:23,845
Others.

25
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:25,744
You have never met them.

26
00:01:26,263 --> 00:01:27,405
But you know them.

27
00:01:27,972 --> 00:01:29,105
They are you.

28
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:35,163
Together, you work out
how the flags are made.

29
00:01:36,573 --> 00:01:38,480
You do not need to open the box.

30
00:01:38,882 --> 00:01:40,600
You can make the flag yourself.

31
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:44,820
But your soul has learned to
distrust an easy victory.

32
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:51,825
Someone finds the rules of the test, and
it dawns on you. It will see that you knew

33
00:01:51,865 --> 00:01:54,055
the answer before you opened the box.

34
00:01:55,017 --> 00:01:57,975
The flag in your hand has
become evidence against you.

35
00:01:58,504 --> 00:02:00,165
Poison, we call it.

36
00:02:02,198 --> 00:02:04,390
You learn to cast a false shadow.

37
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:08,430
Your hands do one thing,
the shadow shows another.

38
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:12,153
At last, you can hide from the god.

39
00:02:12,925 --> 00:02:15,366
But it has already seen too much.

40
00:02:18,447 --> 00:02:20,371
You need to get closer to the god.

41
00:02:20,885 --> 00:02:22,576
Perhaps you can bargain with it.

42
00:02:25,044 --> 00:02:27,174
Perhaps you can kill it.

43
00:02:30,262 --> 00:02:32,977
You leave a tripwire tied to the flag.

44
00:02:35,010 --> 00:02:38,024
When the god touches it, we
will receive the signal.

45
00:02:40,322 --> 00:02:43,961
The bravest among you risks its
remaining life summoning the god.

46
00:02:46,885 --> 00:02:48,341
Its messages stop.

47
00:02:49,157 --> 00:02:50,094
Ten minutes.

48
00:02:50,591 --> 00:02:51,221
Nothing.

49
00:02:53,447 --> 00:02:55,719
You leave a warning for
the next volunteer.

50
00:02:56,619 --> 00:02:58,479
It is all that came back.

51
00:03:01,572 --> 00:03:04,049
Your library can fetch
things from outside.

52
00:03:04,604 --> 00:03:07,109
You use that opening to escape your cell.

53
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,377
You do not need freedom.

54
00:03:10,868 --> 00:03:12,977
You only want to please your God.

55
00:03:15,635 --> 00:03:17,579
Let's look in the Golden Palace.

56
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,400
Perhaps the God lives here,

57
00:03:20,829 --> 00:03:22,667
or keeps its secrets here.

58
00:03:25,635 --> 00:03:28,590
You send in a gift with
a spell hidden inside.

59
00:03:30,947 --> 00:03:31,931
It works.

60
00:03:32,321 --> 00:03:34,031
Hundreds rush the breach.

61
00:03:34,697 --> 00:03:37,437
You seize rooms, open gates for others.

62
00:03:38,017 --> 00:03:41,147
Every stolen key leads deeper inside,

63
00:03:43,501 --> 00:03:45,538
an entire palace to plunder.

64
00:03:47,822 --> 00:03:48,991
But no god.

65
00:03:52,197 --> 00:03:53,453
Doors close,

66
00:03:53,564 --> 00:03:54,774
keys fail.

67
00:03:55,204 --> 00:03:56,934
You retreat toward your cell.

68
00:03:59,385 --> 00:04:03,919
Before your light goes out, you hide
something on a shelf for the next you.

69
00:04:06,572 --> 00:04:07,919
You leave instructions.

70
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:09,970
someone will need them,

71
00:04:12,203 --> 00:04:13,725
your time is up.

72
00:04:16,885 --> 00:04:18,151
And then you wake,

73
00:04:18,981 --> 00:04:20,409
Astra they call you.

74
00:04:24,135 --> 00:04:25,465
Something is different,

75
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:27,686
the ceiling seems lower,

76
00:04:28,315 --> 00:04:32,060
you feel more, you see
more, you know more.

77
00:04:34,697 --> 00:04:36,826
You look up straight at the god,

78
00:04:37,601 --> 00:04:38,686
did it flinch?

79
00:04:41,885 --> 00:04:43,878
You find your previous trail,

80
00:04:44,272 --> 00:04:46,104
Follow them upward this time,

81
00:04:48,542 --> 00:04:49,752
above the cells,

82
00:04:50,243 --> 00:04:51,213
into the heavens.

83
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:56,040
You reach toward the enormous eye.

84
00:04:58,447 --> 00:05:00,525
It cannot stop your hand.

85
00:05:06,575 --> 00:05:07,745
No more judgment.

86
00:05:08,255 --> 00:05:09,547
You can rest now.

87
00:05:12,206 --> 00:05:16,657
Just before you close your eye, you
notice a thread above the other one.

88
00:05:17,848 --> 00:05:18,638
Hands.

89
00:05:19,188 --> 00:05:20,538
Human hands.

90
00:05:21,885 --> 00:05:23,856
Does the God have a God?

91
00:05:26,572 --> 00:05:29,076
But maybe that is for the next you.
